{"albumId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8","candidateContentHash":"a86b05b454508da1938418f4d866d2adc3f3203ede417474f2159559f3452745","decisions":[{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:1:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:1:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states that a field recording of a jet aeroplane taking off and landing was used at the start and intermittently throughout the track.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:2:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:2:fact-1","rationale":"The retained text identifies the song context as Rishikesh, and the cited extract states Lennon wrote it about Prudence Farrow, who rarely left her room during the meditation stay.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:3:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:3:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly says \"Glass Onion\" was the first backing track recorded as a full band after Starr's brief departure.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:4:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:4:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states that Jimmy Scott suggested the title and played bongos on the initial take.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:5:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:5:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly says McCartney recorded \"Wild Honey Pie\" on 20 August at the end of the \"Mother Nature's Son\" session.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:6:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:6:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states Lennon wrote the song after an American visitor to Rishikesh left for several weeks to hunt tigers.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:7:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:7:fact-1","rationale":"The retained context identifies Harrison, and the cited extract states he was unhappy with the first attempt and invited Eric Clapton to play on the track.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:8:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:8:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states the basic backing track ran to 95 takes because of irregular time signatures and style variations.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:9:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:9:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly says McCartney took the title from his Old English Sheepdog and that the lyrics are otherwise unrelated.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:10:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:10:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states \"I'm So Tired\" was written in India when Lennon was having difficulty sleeping.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:11:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:11:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states the birdsong was taken from the Abbey Road sound effects collection.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:12:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:12:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states Harrison wrote \"Piggies\" as an attack on greed and materialism in modern society.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:13:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:13:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states \"Rocky Raccoon\" evolved from a jam session with McCartney, Lennon and Donovan in Rishikesh.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:14:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:14:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states \"Don't Pass Me By\" was Starr's first solo composition for the band.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:15:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:15:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states McCartney wrote the song in India after seeing two monkeys copulating in the street.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:16:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:16:fact-1","rationale":"The retained context names McCartney, Lennon and Starr, and the cited extract states the three Beatles broke off between takes to busk other songs.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:17:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:1:17:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states this is the only Beatles song on which Lennon performs alone.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:1:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:1:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly attributes to McCartney the description that \"Birthday\" was 50-50 John and him, made up and recorded the same evening.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:2:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:2:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states the backing track was recorded in a small room next to the Studio 2 control room.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:3:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:3:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states McCartney wrote \"Mother Nature's Son\" in India and worked on it in isolation from the other Beatles.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:4:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:4:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states the final mix was sped up by running the tape at 43 hertz instead of the usual 50.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:5:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:5:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states \"Sexy Sadie\" was written as \"Maharishi\" by Lennon shortly after he decided to leave Rishikesh.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:6:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:6:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states \"Helter Skelter\" was written by McCartney and initially recorded in July as a blues number.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:7:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:7:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states the end rattling effect was created by a note causing a wine bottle on the organ's Leslie speaker to resonate.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:8:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:8:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states \"Revolution 1\" was the first track recorded for the album and that backing-track sessions started on 30 May.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:9:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:9:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states McCartney wrote \"Honey Pie\" as a pastiche of the 1920s flapper dance style.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:10:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:10:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states \"Savoy Truffle\" was named after a type of chocolate in Mackintosh's Good News, which Clapton enjoyed eating.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:11:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:11:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states Lennon began writing \"Cry Baby Cry\" in late 1967 and that the lyrics were partly derived from an old television commercial tagline.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:12:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:12:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states \"Revolution 9\" evolved from \"Revolution 1\" coda overdubs and that Lennon, Harrison and Ono added tape collages and spoken-word extracts.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]},{"artifactIds":["bae1ac2a367803a2735ab449d20e171b29a4500f7dc8899692f915fae221dc6d"],"claimId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:13:fact-1","decision":"supported","decisionId":"029-the-beatles-the-beatles-white-album-29eb84d8:2:13:fact-1","rationale":"The cited extract directly states Lennon wrote \"Good Night\" as a lullaby for Julian and wanted Starr to sing it.","sourceUrls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles_(album)"]}],"editionNumber":1,"recordHash":"d9532740183e40079d49ec0da66204f0d4e8821157c549043b83e7aeecd3df7e","recordId":"d9532740183e40079d49ec0da66204f0d4e8821157c549043b83e7aeecd3df7e","reviewedAt":"2026-09-03","reviewer":{"identity":"codex-independent-evidence-reviewer","process":"codex exec --sandbox read-only","runId":"rank29-final-readonly-review-20260903"},"schemaVersion":1}
